--- task
id: t15
dataset: section8
kind: count per group

--- intent
For each company that has employees, return its name and its number of employees as `n`, largest first.

--- edition2
query headcount() {
  match { $c: Company  $p worksAt $c }
  return { $c.name, count($p) as n }
  order { n desc }
}

--- edition3
query headcount() {
  match { $c: Company  $p worksAt $c }
  return { $c.name, count($p) as n }
  order { n desc }
}

--- edition3
query headcount() {
  match { $p worksAt $c }
  return { $c.name, count($p) as n }
  order { n desc }
}

--- expect ordered
columns: ["c.name","n"]
["Acme",3]
["Globex",1]

--- note
Grouping drops a company with no employees; the intent names only companies that have employees, so the grouped form and the count-block form differ on no row the task asks for.
